# LSTM pipeline generated artifacts — regenerated by pipeline.py each run.
# Paths are relative to this lstm_pipeline/ directory.

# Trained models (per-RSU + global .pt weights, ~46 MB) — tracked so
# teammates can pull them without rerunning the pipeline.
models_backup_*/

# Preprocessed windows / labels / meta (.npy arrays, ~35 MB)
preprocessed/

# Per-run pipeline outputs. NOTE (2026-08-08, LSTM_PIPELINE_AUDIT): scaler_params.json,
# fed_summary.json, hparams.json and evaluation_results.json are the PROVENANCE of
# lstm_weights_cpp.bin, not scratch — they are the only record of what scaler/theta/
# hparams a given .bin was exported under. Ignoring them let the committed .bin and
# these files drift out of sync with nothing to catch it (see audit §2/§5). Keep them
# tracked and commit them alongside any new lstm_weights_cpp.bin export.
local_results.json
poison_sweep_results.json

# Kept tracked (do NOT ignore): the calibration deliverable, small and
# referenced by scratch/s1_detection.h and scratch/routing.cc —
#   calibrated_params.json
#   calibration_report.txt
